id: decisions/049-source-admissibility
title: "Three kinds of source, each checked its own way"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'source-admissibility'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: source-admissibility
axis_gloss: "whether only material already inside the tree may be cited as backing, or outside artifacts and services count"
poles:
  a: outside-source-admitted
  b: repo-internal-source
split: genuinely-split
draft_status: full
leverage: 2
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(2) x split_weight(1) x authored_conflict_bonus(1)"

question: >
  What may a record name as its source — only other .yawn records, any file in
  this tree, or things outside it (a paper, a DOI, a service, a file on the
  operator's machine) — and how does a reader check each kind?

why_it_matters: >
  Today a .sql file, a DOI and a path on Dave's laptop are all written the same
  way under source:, and the validator resolves one kind, silently skips another
  and grandfathers the third; the manifest names ten outside disciplines as
  influences and cites fifteen files, every one inside the tree. Once answered,
  every child Yawn and bot below Dave learns which of the three kinds it may
  cite and at what proof status, and a reader can tell at a glance which sources
  open from the tree.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    1 judgments sit at outside-source-admitted (0 authored) and 1 at
    repo-internal-source (0 authored). The repository asserts both directions on
    this axis.
  attributed_to: JUDGMENTS.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    Whether Dave wants external works citable under source: at all, or only in
    references/ prose; and whether the two grandfathered operator-path proofs
    should be vendored, downgraded, or kept as historical receipts.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      rule: Outside sources admitted. A source: or proof.source entry may be
      anything a reader could in principle consult — a tree file of any type, a DOI
      or URL, an operator path — provided the entry says which kind it is.
      yawn.yawn's source list adds the external works its influence_frame names.
    cost: "Type every source entry by prefix; extend scripts/validate-proof-refs.mjs to check well-formedness of DOIs and URLs and to require each be listed in references/source-index.yawn; add .sql and other tracked extensions to its path pattern."
    risk: "Unreachable sources (a URL that moves, a path on one machine) carry the same weight as a file in the tree, and a proof.status of source-backed means less than it looks."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "Extend scripts/validate-proof-refs.mjs: tree paths must resolve (any tracked extension, .sql included); https and doi entries must be well-formed and appear in references/source-index.yawn; drive-letter paths are reported under the existing shrink-only ledger."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0352"
  - name: B
    description: >
      rule: Repo-internal only. A source: names only a file in this tree. External
      works are cited in references/ prose with author, year and DOI but never as
      proof.source; operator paths are removed by vendoring the file or marking the
      claim unverified, which the validator already demands for new ones.
    cost: "Vendor or downgrade the two grandfathered external proofs (references/july-01-lock.yawn, references/scientific-frame.yawn); reject URLs under proof:; the manifest's influence_frame stays a list of disciplines with no citable works."
    risk: "A protocol that names ten outside disciplines as its lineage can never cite them as sources, so lineage lives only in prose and the credit-the-whole-lineage decision has nowhere to put a DOI."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "scripts/validate-proof-refs.mjs rejects any https or doi entry under proof:, extends its path pattern to every tracked extension, and its external ceiling goes from 2 to 0 once the two grandfathered files vendor or downgrade."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0766"
  - name: C
    description: >
      rule: Three admissible kinds of source, each with its own check, written in
      templates/proof.yawn. tree_ref: any tracked file of any extension, must
      resolve. external_ref: a DOI or URL, admissible as reference lineage and under
      source: but not as proof — it cannot raise proof.status above source-backed.
      operator_ref: a path outside the tree, never admissible as proof or source;
      allowed only as an automation's workspace_ref (see runtime-dependence).
      yawn.yawn's source list keeps its tree refs; its influence_frame disciplines
      resolve to external_refs in references/source-index.yawn.
    cost: "Three prefixes documented in templates/proof.yawn; scripts/validate-proof-refs.mjs extended for .sql and for the external-ref status ceiling; references/source-index.yawn gains one cited work per discipline in influence_frame."
    risk: "The status ceiling for external refs is argued around ('the DOI is the proof') and the validator cannot tell a citation from a claim."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "Extend scripts/validate-proof-refs.mjs: add .sql and every tracked extension to its path pattern; reject an https or doi entry under proof: when proof.status is above source-backed; keep the drive-letter ledger at ceiling 2 and shrinking; a test that references/source-index.yawn names at least one work for each discipline in yawn.yawn influence_frame."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0352"
      - "J0766"

recommendation:
  option_ref: C
  confidence: 0.6
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    This is close and thin: one REVEALED judgment on each side, nothing authored,
    and the two artifacts do not even contradict each other — one cites an in-tree
    .sql beside .yawn files and grades itself seed-backed, the other omits the
    outside literature its own influence_frame names. What tips it is what the
    passing validator already implements: scripts/validate-proof-refs.mjs resolves
    tree paths (but its extension list omits .sql, so J0352's citation is checked
    by nothing), reports drive-letter paths under a shrink-only ledger of two, and
    silently admits https URLs — the last is the gap. So the tree has already
    chosen a typed answer for two of three kinds and left the third unspoken. C
    names all three and puts a status ceiling on the one the validator cannot
    open. The neighbouring evidence-locus decision (proof-reaches-outside) asks
    whether proof must reach beyond the .yawn graph; this one only asks what a
    source may be and how each kind is checked, and C answers by typing rather
    than admitting or banning wholesale. Low-moderate confidence because both
    judgments are readings, not preferences.

target_condition:
  mode: decide
  proposed_by: agent-on-behalf
  affected_principals:
    - principal:dave
  ratification_status: proposed
  sufficient_when:
    - "templates/proof.yawn documents tree_ref, external_ref and operator_ref and the proof status each may support."
    - "scripts/validate-proof-refs.mjs checks .sql and every other tracked extension, and fails when an https or doi entry sits under a proof: whose status is above source-backed."
    - "references/source-index.yawn names at least one work for each discipline in yawn.yawn influence_frame, and a test checks the mapping."

choice:
  selected_by: ""
  option_ref: ""
  authority_ref: ""

proof:
  covers:
    - target_condition
    - options
  falsifier: >
    A proof block cites an https URL and reports production-verified while nothing
    resolves the URL and the validator passes; or a .sql citation goes unchecked
    because the validator's extension list still omits it.
  status: proposed

resolves:
  - "J0352"
  - "J0766"

boundary:
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective; this record proposes and Dave decides"
  - "the REVEALED judgments cited here describe what artifacts do, not what Dave chose"

source:
  template: templates/decision.yawn
  axis: TAXONOMY.md
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
